WEBVTT

00:01:29.927 --> 00:01:33.177
I was told the story that Mozart,
just before he'd go to bed,

00:01:33.201 --> 00:01:34.587
he'd go to the piano and go,

00:01:34.611 --> 00:01:35.765
"da-da-da-da-da."

00:01:35.789 --> 00:01:38.472
His father, who was already in bed,
would think, "Argh."

00:01:38.496 --> 00:01:41.188
He'd have to get up
and hit the final note to the chord

00:01:41.212 --> 00:01:42.816
before he could go back to sleep.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:43.934
(Laughter)

00:01:43.958 --> 00:01:49.059
So the need for closure
leads us to thinking about:

00:01:49.083 --> 00:01:51.260
What is our greatest fear?

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:56.642
Think -- what is our greatest fear
growing up, even now?

00:01:57.407 --> 00:02:01.064
And it's the fear of the dark.